{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109500","id":2733697171,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6i8OiT","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109500","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109500.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109500.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109500","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109500/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109500/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109500/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/6d7fac731290ab3745815056736a8c4c1c668857","number":109500,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add PipeWire camera feeds","user":{"login":"j20001970","id":71766835,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNzY2ODM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71766835?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970","html_url":"https://github.com/j20001970","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/j20001970/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/code_style_guidelines.html\r\n-->\r\nThis PR provides PipeWire camera feeds on linuxbsd platform.\r\n\r\nThe benefits of using PipeWire for camera devices include:\r\n\r\n- Not having to use V4L2 kernel API directly. Access to video devices via V4L2 is exclusive (i.e. Other V4L2/PipeWire clients cannot access the webcam while it is already opened with V4L2), using PipeWire for webcam capture allow multiple clients sharing the webcam.\r\n- Better integration with desktop environments. (For example: camera indicator on KDE Plasma)\r\n- Sandboxed camera access is possible by using [XDG Desktop Portal](https://flatpak.github.io/xdg-desktop-portal).\r\n- _BSD support_, this one is not confirmed yet, but since PipeWire can run on FreeBSD, it is possible to enable camera feeds support with PipeWire that otherwise requires V4L compatibility to build or run camera module.\r\n\r\nCamera feed driver on linuxbsd will be selected at runtime, and fallback to V4L2 driver if failed to initialize PipeWire.\r\n\r\n## Vendored PipeWire headers\r\nThis PR introduces new thirdparty headers to enable PipeWire support. A brief list of added PipeWire and SPA headers **as of version 1.0.0** (the list may change if we update the headers in future) is documented to give a better grasp on how these headers are included (no pun intended).\r\n\r\n```\r\nRequired by \"pipewire/pipewire.h\":\r\n|───\"pipewire/array.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/client.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/conf.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/context.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/device.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/buffers.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/core.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/factory.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/keys.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/log.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/loop.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/link.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/main-loop.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/map.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/mem.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/module.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/node.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/properties.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/proxy.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/permission.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/protocol.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/port.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/stream.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/filter.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/thread-loop.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/data-loop.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/type.h\"\r\n|───\"pipewire/utils.h\"\r\n└───\"pipewire/version.h\"\r\n\r\nSPA headers required by PipeWire:\r\n|───\"spa/buffer/buffer.h\"\r\n|   └───\"spa/buffer/meta.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/node/command.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/node/io.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/node/node.h\"\r\n|   └───\"spa/node/event.h\"\r\n|       └───\"spa/pod/event.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/param/param.h\"\r\n|   |───\"spa/param/buffers.h\"\r\n|   |───\"spa/param/port-config.h\"\r\n|   |───\"spa/param/profile.h\"\r\n|   └───\"spa/param/route.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/pod/command.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/pod/pod.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/support/log.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/support/loop.h\"\r\n|   └───\"spa/support/system.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/support/plugin.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/support/thread.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/utils/defs.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/utils/dict.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/utils/hook.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/utils/list.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/utils/string.h\"\r\n└───\"spa/utils/type.h\"\r\n\r\nHeaders required by `CameraPipeWire`:\r\n└───\"spa/utils/keys.h\" <- for `SPA_KEY_MEDIA_CLASS` and `SPA_KEY_MEDIA_ROLE`\r\n\r\nHeaders required by `CameraFeedPipeWire`:\r\n|───\"spa/param/format.h\" <- for SPA_MEDIA_TYPE_*, SPA_MEDIA_SUBTYPE_* and SPA_FORMAT_VIDEO_* enum\r\n|───\"spa/param/format-utils.h\" <- for spa_format_parse\r\n|   └───\"spa/pod/parser.h\" <- for spa_pod_parse_object\r\n|       |───\"spa/pod/iter.h\"\r\n|       └───\"spa/pod/vararg.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/param/video/mjpg-utils.h\" <- for spa_format_video_mjpg_parse\r\n|   └─── \"spa/param/video/mjpg.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/param/video/raw-utils.h\" <- for spa_format_video_raw_parse\r\n|   └───\"spa/param/video/raw.h\" <- for SPA_VIDEO_FORMAT_* enum\r\n|       |───\"spa/param/video/chroma.h\"\r\n|       |───\"spa/param/video/color.h\"\r\n|       └───\"spa/param/video/multiview.h\"\r\n|───\"spa/param/video/raw-types.h\" <- for spa_type_video_format\r\n└───\"spa/pod/builder.h\" <- for spa pod builder related functions and macros\r\n```\r\n\r\nTODO:\r\n\r\n- [x] Use XDG desktop portal to request camera permission when setting `monitoring_feeds` to true (supersede #100396)\r\n- [x] Use sowrap\r\n- [x] Select PipeWire or V4L2 driver at runtime\r\n- [x] Add support for planar YUV 420 format (Done but no hardware to test)\r\n- [x] Test with more camera feed demo projects\r\n&nbsp;Tested with the following shader:\r\n```gdshader\r\nshader_type canvas_item;\r\n\r\nconst mat3 yuv2rgb_bt709 = mat3(\r\n\tvec3(1.00000, 1.00000, 1.00000),\r\n\tvec3(0.00000, -0.21482, 2.12798),\r\n\tvec3(1.28033, -0.38059, 0.00000)\r\n);\r\n\r\nuniform sampler2D texture_yuy2;\r\n\r\nvoid fragment() {\r\n\tvec2 size = TEXTURE_PIXEL_SIZE;\r\n\tvec2 UV_u = UV - floor(mod(UV / size, 2)) * vec2(1, 0) * size;\r\n\tvec2 UV_v = UV + (vec2(1, 0) - floor(mod(UV / size, 2))) * vec2(1, 0) * size;\r\n\tfloat y = texture(texture_yuy2, UV).r;\r\n\tfloat u = texture(texture_yuy2, UV_u).g;\r\n\tfloat v = texture(texture_yuy2, UV_v).g;\r\n\tvec3 rgb = yuv2rgb_bt709 * vec3(y, u - 0.5, v - 0.5);\r\n\tCOLOR = vec4(rgb, 1.0);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n&nbsp;Tested with [godot-camerafeed-demo](https://github.com/shiena/godot-camerafeed-demo).","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097326,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTczMjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:linuxbsd","name":"platform:linuxbsd","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.g